# Feature Module Conventions

Ported from `.claude/rules/nest-modules.md`, scoped identically across the six NestJS backend
services. `modules/health` is currently the only seeded module in each service — this rule applies
to the first real feature module and every one after it.

## Anatomy

```
src/modules/<name>/
  <name>.module.ts        # controllers + providers only
  <name>.controller.ts    # routing only, no business logic
  <name>.service.ts       # business logic + all DB access
  <name>.swagger.ts       # composite Swagger decorators
  dto/                    # create-<name>.dto.ts, update-<name>.dto.ts
  entities/               # <name>.entity.ts — Swagger response types
  __tests__/              # unit specs (NOT next to source files)
```

Scaffold with `nest g resource modules/<name> --no-spec` (CLI registers the module in
`app.module.ts` automatically), then reshape to this anatomy.

## Controller — thin

- Only routing concerns: `@Param('id', ParseUUIDPipe)`, `@HttpCode(HttpStatus.NO_CONTENT)` on
  delete, delegating to the service
- NO raw `@Api*` decorators on methods — use one composite `@Swagger<Action>()` per method from
  `<name>.swagger.ts`; `@ApiTags` stays on the class

## Swagger composites (`<name>.swagger.ts`)

```ts
export const SwaggerCreateX = () =>
  applyDecorators(
    ApiCreatedResponse({ type: XEntity }),
    ApiConflictResponse({ description: 'Already exists' }),
  );
```

## Service — owns logic and DB access (services that have a database)

- Inject `PrismaService` (global module, no import needed in the feature module) — not applicable
  to `bff`, which has no database; its services compose calls to the domain services instead
- Map known Prisma errors to HTTP exceptions in a private `rethrowKnownErrors(error: unknown): never`:
  `P2002` → `ConflictException`, `P2025` → `NotFoundException`; rethrow everything else
- `findOne` checks for `null` and throws `NotFoundException`

## DTO / Entity

- DTO: class-validator decorators + `@ApiProperty`/`@ApiPropertyOptional`; required fields
  declared with `!`
- Update DTO: `extends PartialType(CreateXDto)` imported from `@nestjs/swagger` (keeps fields
  visible in docs)
- Entity: `class XEntity implements X` with the model type from `src/generated/prisma/client`
  (DB-owning services only), `@ApiProperty` on every field — used as `type:` in Swagger responses

## Unit tests (`__tests__/`)

- Mock dependencies via DI: `{ provide: PrismaService, useValue: { <model>: { create: jest.fn(), ... } } }`
- Test service happy paths + Prisma error mapping (P2002→409, P2025→404); controller tests just
  verify delegation
